tm_medium=reader2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Feb 2026 13:03:26 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why Evolutionary Psychology Needs Behavior Genetics, and Vice Versa]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.stevestewartwilliams.com/p/why-evolutionary-psychology-needs?utm_source=%2Finbox&utm_medium=reader2">https://www.stevestewartwilliams.com/p/why-evolutionary-psychology-needs?utm_source=%2Finbox&utm_medium=reader2</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/political-psychology-links-2152026">Political Psychology Links, 2/17/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.stevestewartwilliams.com/p/why-evolutionary-psychology-needs?utm_source=%2Finbox&amp;utm_medium=reader2</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.stevestewartwilliams.com/p/why-evolutionary-psychology-needs?utm_source=%2Finbox&amp;utm_medium=reader2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Feb 2026 13:03:26 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why Bitcoin Is Crashing]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.thefp.com/p/why-bitcoin-is-crashing">https://www.thefp.com/p/why-bitcoin-is-crashing</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/economics-links-2162026">Economics Links, 2/16/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.thefp.com/p/why-bitcoin-is-crashing</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.thefp.com/p/why-bitcoin-is-crashing</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Feb 2026 13:03:23 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why Evolutionary Psychology Needs Behavior Genetics, and Vice Versa]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>In Case You Missed It…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://www.stevestewartwilliams.com/p/why-evolutionary-psychology-needs?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://www.stevestewartwilliams.com/p/why-evolutionary-psychology-needs?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/political-psychology-links-2152026">Political Psychology Links, 2/17/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.stevestewartwilliams.com/p/why-evolutionary-psychology-needs?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.stevestewartwilliams.com/p/why-evolutionary-psychology-needs?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Feb 2026 13:03:26 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Left-Progressivism’s Three Foundational Falsehoods]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>Universities across Anglo-America, and across the West more broadly, have become increasingly dominated by a Critical Theory magisterium: a teaching authority that claims ultimate or trumping moral authority. This magisterium is based on Critical Theory and its derivatives…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://www.lorenzofromoz.net/p/left-progressivisms-three-foundational?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://www.lorenzofromoz.net/p/left-progressivisms-three-foundational?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/political-psychology-links-2152026">Political Psychology Links, 2/17/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.lorenzofromoz.net/p/left-progressivisms-three-foundational?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.lorenzofromoz.net/p/left-progressivisms-three-foundational?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Feb 2026 13:03:26 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why Have Academics Failed To Study Social Justice Ideology?]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>This is a guest post by Thomas Prosser (who writes at The Path Not Taken) and Edmund King (who writes at Paroxysms) about their very interesting new book, Beyond Woke and Anti-Woke: Explaining the Rise of Social Justice Ideology…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://www.conspicuouscognition.com/p/why-have-academics-failed-to-study?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://www.conspicuouscognition.com/p/why-have-academics-failed-to-study?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/political-psychology-links-2152026">Political Psychology Links, 2/17/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.conspicuouscognition.com/p/why-have-academics-failed-to-study?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.conspicuouscognition.com/p/why-have-academics-failed-to-study?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Feb 2026 13:03:26 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why Economists Linearize Everything]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>In 2012, Melissa Dell, Benjamin Jones, and Benjamin Olken published an influential paper on temperature and economic growth. It was a landmark contribution: the first rigorous panel study to use within-country temperature fluctuations to identify causal effects on aggregate output, and it opened entirely new channels, showing that temperature affects not just agriculture but industrial output, political stability, and capital accumulation. They ran a linear regression, GDP growth on temperature shocks, with country fixed effects and the standard controls. They even tested for nonlinear effects, but found little evidence at the macro level. Crucially, though, their tests were conducted within a linear framework: they checked whether the linear slope differed across subgroups, hot versus cold countries, rich versus poor, but never asked whether the relationship itself was curved. For rich countries clustered near the peak of what would turn out to be an inverted-U, the positive effects …</p><p>URL: <a href="https://carloschavezp29.substack.com/p/why-economists-linearize-everything?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web">https://carloschavezp29.substack.com/p/why-economists-linearize-everything?utm_source=substack&utm_campaign=post_embed&utm_medium=web</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://arnoldkling.substack.com/p/economics-links-2162026">Economics Links, 2/16/2026</a></p>]]></description><link>https://carloschavezp29.substack.com/p/why-economists-linearize-everything?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://carloschavezp29.substack.com/p/why-economists-linearize-everything?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_campaign=post_embed&amp;utm_medium=web</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Feb 2026 13:03:23 GMT</pubDate></item></channel></rss>